<title>GERMANY: Pan-German June adjusted jobless rises 11,000. [CORRECTED 09:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Pan-German June adjusted jobless rises 11,000. [CORRECTED 09:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   June 97     May 97	   June 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)		4.222 million   4.256 million	3.785 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		  4.374 million   4.363 million	3.925 million</p>
<p> Change in adj number	+11,000     +55,000	  unch</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		  11.0 pct    11.1 pct	 9.9 pct</p>
<p>(Corrects June unemployment rate to 11.0 pct from 11.1 pct)</p>
<p> Short-time workers	  167,668     183,339	  275,394</p>
<p> Vacancies (unadj)	   366,897     360,628	  366,057</p>
<p> Change in numbers in work Apr 97	Mar 97</p>
<p>				  - 18,000     +43,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
